@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@
+---
+name: setting-up-tracking-providers
+description: Use in a primary interactive session when a version-controlled repository first uses Sjujperpowers without .sjujperpowers/config.json, or when the user asks to configure Plane, file-roadmap, Kata, or session tracking backends.
+---
+
+# Setting Up Tracking Providers
+
+## Scope
+
+Run this once per repository before the first roadmap, spec, plan, issue, or
+Jujutsu mutation. Do not run it in subagents or non-interactive jobs. Do not
+silently accept the default `file + session` combination on first interactive
+use: those defaults remain valid, but the operator must choose them knowingly.
+
+This skill configures provider references and verifies access. Agents reuse an
+existing Plane project when one fits or create a standalone project directly
+with the standard feature profile. Project visibility is not an onboarding gate.
+
+## 1. Inspect before asking
+
+Run `jj root`. If it fails, stop:
+
+> This isn't a jj repo. Run `jj git init --colocate` and re-run, or tell me to continue without VCS steps.
+
+Never invoke the resolver with an empty `--root` value. After the operator
+initializes the colocated repository, set `root="$(jj root)"`. If the operator
+instead explicitly chooses to continue without VCS steps, set
+`root="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"` and skip all Jujutsu operations.
+
+Resolve the current provider state with that explicit root:
+
+```bash
+node <tracking-providers skill dir>/scripts/resolve-config.mjs \
+  --root "$root"
+```
+
+If `configPath` is non-null, report the resolved providers and stop unless the
+operator explicitly asked to reconfigure them.
+
+When no configuration exists, inspect before asking:
+
+1. Existing project documentation and established docs root.
+2. Available Plane projects through a mounted Plane tool or the constrained
+   `plane-api` command.
+3. `kata health --json` and `kata projects list --json`.
+4. Repository landing convention: local landing or pull request.
+
+Never request, read, print, or persist a credential. A missing Plane tool,
+missing non-secret placeholder, or `401`/`403` means Plane is unavailable in
+this agent environment; report that boundary instead of silently choosing a
+different provider.
+
+## 2. Ask only for real provider decisions
+
+Ask the operator for the choices that inspection cannot determine:
+
+- Roadmap: `plane`, `file`, or `none`.
+- Execution: `kata`, `session`, or `none`.
+- Completion boundary for Kata: `landed` or `pull_request`.
+- Existing Plane product/platform project when one fits; otherwise the agent creates a standalone project.
+- Kata project name when no matching project exists.
+
+Infer `docsRoot` from repository convention. Ask only when multiple established
+locations are plausible. Plane and Kata are independent; never imply that one
+requires the other.
+
+## 3. Preflight selected backends
+
+For Plane, make a harmless authenticated project-list request through the
+available Plane tool or:
+
+```bash
+plane-api GET '/api/v1/workspaces/<workspace>/projects/?per_page=100'
+```
+
+If the operator selected Plane and this preflight reports missing access, use
+the environment's credential-provisioning skill to give the operator scoped
+hidden-entry commands, then stop. Resume setup only after the operator reports
+that access is active.
+
+Reuse an existing Plane project when the repository belongs to that product or
+platform. For a standalone product with no match, infer a concise project name
+and uppercase identifier from repository context. Ask only when either value is
+ambiguous or conflicts with an existing project. Otherwise create it directly:
+
+```bash
+name='PROJECT NAME'
+identifier='IDENTIFIER'
+plane-api POST "/api/v1/workspaces/<workspace>/projects/" \
+  "$(jq -cn \
+    --arg name "$name" \
+    --arg identifier "$identifier" \
+    '{name:$name, identifier:$identifier, module_view:true,
+      cycle_view:false, issue_views_view:true, page_view:true,
+      intake_view:true}')"
+```
+
+This standard profile enables modules, views, pages, and intake while leaving
+cycles disabled. Separate MCP feature routes return 404, but Plane `1.4.2`
+accepts these fields in its project create and update serializers. Use Plane's
+default visibility; Secret visibility is not required. Retrieve the created
+project and continue without delegating UI setup to the operator.
+
+For Kata:
+
+```bash
+kata health --json
+kata projects show <project> --json
+```
+
+If the selected project does not exist, create it once and then resolve it:
+
+```bash
+kata projects create <project> --json
+kata projects show <project> --json
+```
+
+Do not write `.sjujperpowers/config.json` until every selected runtime backend
+passes its preflight.
+
+## 4. Persist one validated configuration
+
+Run the configurator from this skill directory. Example:
+
+```bash
+node <setting-up-tracking-providers skill dir>/scripts/configure-providers.mjs \
+  --root "$root" \
+  --docs-root docs/project \
+  --roadmap plane \
+  --roadmap-project 'Example Product' \
+  --execution kata \
+  --execution-project example-product \
+  --completion landed
+```
+
+Use `--overwrite` only after showing the existing resolved configuration and
+receiving an explicit reconfiguration request. The command validates the
+closed schema, preflights Kata when selected, and atomically writes the file.
+
+## 5. Verify and continue
+
+Run checked resolution again:
+
+```bash
+node <tracking-providers skill dir>/scripts/resolve-config.mjs \
+  --root "$root"
+```
+
+Report the roadmap provider, execution provider, docs root, and completion
+boundary. Then return to the lifecycle skill that triggered setup. The new
+configuration is versioned project policy and belongs in that change.
